




Modelling the fluxes and Riemann solvers with SymPy
---------------------------------------------------

You can model your fluxes, Riemann solvers and so forth with SymPy,
i.e. through symbolic formulations---as long as you use a generic
numerical Riemann solver such as Rusanov. The  SymPy wrapper is held
within the  subpackage `exahype2.sympy`.

I provide a couple of classes for different PDE variants that should be
compatible to particular  Finite Volume and ADER-DG solvers. All SymPy
classes wrap around SymPy's symbolic expressions, and thus allow users
to work with these expressions directly. Once you have finished you
modelling, the wrappers offer some code generation which again decorate
SymPy's code generation, adds some glue code and can inject the generate
into a  solver.

